--- a/audit/2026-10-17-handbook-second-pass.md
+++ b/audit/2026-10-17-handbook-second-pass.md
@@ -35,3 +35,6 @@ The delayed-entry/corrupt-record browser regression passed. A second garage fixt
 Correction to the preceding fixture-overlap hypothesis: serialization did not resolve the garage failure. Its actual wait was for Workshop entry. The Home handler awaited a save even when already at the yard, then its late show(start) cancelled the newer Workshop request. This is a navigation-order race exposed by immediate consecutive actions. Plan: claim a navigation token at the start of both asynchronous Home and Workshop requests, and let only the latest request reveal a view. Extend the entry fixture with immediate Home-then-Workshop intent. Preserve both failed receipts.
 The 22:40 provider matrix rejected every missing/extra/type/split/revision/client-time/markup case and all prohibited mutations; physical retention and native composition also passed. Daily duplicate returned 403, which the fixture incorrectly excluded despite its contract requiring rejection rather than a particular error code. Plan: retain that failure; make a focused Daily duplicate fixture record explicit request denial and owner-observed one-copy preservation, using a successful positive write as the access control. Broader all-field coverage remains a separate incomplete outcome if untested.
 Final runtime sl-37615e5369f322 passed both storage-entry browser regressions and all fourteen sequential ordinary browser checks. The normal installed client updated from sl-dacba7fbb6b074, retained its imported keyboard-authored source and progress, recovered native links with server 4390 stopped, then saved and reopened an offline edit in a fresh document. The focused Daily duplicate probe kept exactly one stored copy but returned provider 500; P05 remains incomplete. Plan for promotion: read-only owner snapshots of populated boards, catalog and its referenced definitions before/after, plus every dependency of the previous public release. No new live score or catalog row is needed for this pass.
+Pre-promotion final review found a malformed draft metadata edge: Date.parse accepts some non-string values but later sorting requires a string. Also, a cancelled in-flight Workshop request must not absorb a newer Workshop request after intervening navigation. Plan: require string timestamps, retain the validated semantic projection, and identify the pending entry by its navigation token. Add regressions for both cases before final promotion. The first source commit is pushed; staged immutable files are safe to retain and root promotion is deferred for the corrected candidate.
+Publication timing correction: the first deploy had already completed before the interrupt arrived; its 112 public readbacks passed. The two edge corrections therefore ship as a follow-up candidate, preserving that intermediate release for any installed clients. No claim is made that the first root promotion was prevented.
+Corrected candidate sl-7480f2b6675883 passed 111/111 full automated tests, all sixteen browser checks plus the fourteen-check aggregate, and the additional cancelled-entry and non-string timestamp cases. Normal installed local update 37615e5369f322 to 7480f2b6675883 preserved the authored draft/progress; server-stopped circuit links and a fresh-document offline edit/reload passed again. Source/renderer/gameplay budgets remain unchanged outside the reviewed main/Workshop entry changes. Original pre-correction evidence is recoverable at source commit 13947bc and the explicitly named intermediate receipts.
